{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-qmg9-m772-5rm7","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parse-community/parse-server/security-advisories/GHSA-qmg9-m772-5rm7","html_url":"https://github.com/parse-community/parse-server/security/advisories/GHSA-qmg9-m772-5rm7","summary":"Unauthenticated deletion of class schemas removes class-level permissions on MongoDB","description":"### Impact\n\nOn deployments that use MongoDB, a client without the master key can delete the stored schema of any class through the REST API. This removes the class's field definitions, class-level permissions and protected fields, including those set with the `protectedFields` server option. Data protected only by these can then become readable and modifiable by any client, and a class can become inaccessible to clients until it is re-created. Object ACLs continue to apply. Deployments that use PostgreSQL are not affected.\n\n### Patches\n\nClient requests to class names that are not valid class names, including the internal schema collection, are now rejected unless they use the master key or maintenance key.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nRegister a Cloud Code `beforeDelete` trigger for the class name `_SCHEMA` that rejects requests without the master key. Upgrading does not restore schemas that were already deleted; review the class-level permissions, protected fields and field definitions of all classes and restore them where needed.\n\n### References\n\n- GitHub security advisory: https://github.com/parse-community/parse-server/security/advisories/GHSA-qmg9-m772-5rm7\n- Fix Parse Server 9: https://github.com/parse-community/parse-server/pull/10767\n- Fix Parse Server 8: https://github.com/parse-community/parse-server/pull/10768","severity":"high","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"mtrezza","id":5673677,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NzM2Nzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5673677?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtrezza","html_url":"https://github.com/mtrezza","follow